      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Irradiation of the unmodified alloy produces a Cr/V-rich second phase.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The unmodified alloy undergoes only minor or slight irradiation hardening at approximately 8 dpa.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is addition of approximately 0.5–1 at.% Zr to the starting alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Added Zr will preferentially segregate to grain boundaries and irradiation-defect sites.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solute segregation at grain boundaries can stabilize a nanocrystalline HEA and reduce grain-boundary mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4510962::web::011::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Segregated Zr will lower grain-boundary diffusion rates and reduce atomic mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced grain-boundary mobility will suppress the migration and segregation of Cr and V that produces precipitates.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The unmodified alloy exhibits Cr and V segregation at grain boundaries and triple junctions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The unmodified alloy resists irradiation-induced dislocation-loop formation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr microalloying will preserve the alloy's resistance to irradiation-induced defect clustering.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr microalloying will decrease the volume fraction of Cr/V-rich precipitates by more than 50% relative to the unmodified alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr microalloying will retain negligible irradiation hardening.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr microalloying will improve the alloy's suitability for practical bulk fabrication.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention will be effective up to approximately 8 dpa at 500–600 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The cited unmodified alloy was irradiated up to 8 dpa at room temperature and 1073 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr-rich intermetallic phases may form during processing and could embrittle the alloy or otherwise degrade its mechanical properties.",
